exports[`Unit 20 recorded output: area-parallelogram-trapezoid > matches the authored sample output 1`] = `
"--- area-parallelogram-trapezoid · seed 1 · difficulty 1
prompt   Find the area of this trapezoid in square centimetres.
display  geometry area-trapezoid base1 6 base2 8 height 8 unit cm name "Trapezoid with bases 6 cm and 8 cm, and perpendicular height 8 cm" formulas ["A equals b times h" row("A = ", "bh"); "A equals b1 plus b2 times h divided by 2" row("A = ", fraction("(b1 + b2)h", "2"))]
answer   exact 56/1
input    keypad
hint     Use the formula matching the figure.
step 1   Add the two bases.   [6 + 8 = 14]
step 2   Multiply the sum by height.   [14 × 8 = 112]
step 3   Take half the product.   [112 ÷ 2 = 56]

--- area-parallelogram-trapezoid · seed 12345 · difficulty 1
prompt   Find the area of this trapezoid in square metres.
display  geometry area-trapezoid base1 5 base2 7 height 6 unit m name "Trapezoid with bases 5 m and 7 m, and perpendicular height 6 m" formulas ["A equals b times h" row("A = ", "bh"); "A equals b1 plus b2 times h divided by 2" row("A = ", fraction("(b1 + b2)h", "2"))]
answer   exact 36/1
input    keypad
hint     Use the formula matching the figure.
step 1   Add the two bases.   [5 + 7 = 12]
step 2   Multiply the sum by height.   [12 × 6 = 72]
step 3   Take half the product.   [72 ÷ 2 = 36]

--- area-parallelogram-trapezoid · seed 67890 · difficulty 1
prompt   Find the area of this parallelogram in square metres.
display  geometry area-parallelogram base 6 height 5 unit m name "Parallelogram with base 6 m and perpendicular height 5 m" formulas ["A equals b times h" row("A = ", "bh"); "A equals b1 plus b2 times h divided by 2" row("A = ", fraction("(b1 + b2)h", "2"))]
answer   exact 30/1
input    keypad
hint     Use the formula matching the figure.
step 1   Multiply base by perpendicular height.   [6 × 5 = 30]
step 2   Write square metres for area.   [30 square metres]

--- area-parallelogram-trapezoid · seed 424242 · difficulty 1
