display  geometry circumference radius 8 unit cm name "Circle with radius 8 cm" formulas ["C equals pi times d" row("C = ", "πd"); "A equals pi times r squared" row("A = ", row("π", superscript("r", "2")))]
answer   approx 50.2 ±0.05
input    keypad
keypad   allowDecimal=true
hint     Double the radius, then use circumference formula.
step 1   Double the shown radius.   [2 × 8 = 16]
step 2   Multiply diameter by 3.14.   [3.14 × 16 = 50.24]
step 3   Round to the nearest tenth.   [50.2]
miss     radius-as-diameter = 25.1   The formula needs diameter, which is twice the radius.
miss     area-for-circumference = 201   Circumference is not the circle area.

